      "heading": "Poa's role and knowledge",
      "id": "P003",
      "kind": "finding",
      "text": "Poa described his former Dep-Ed roles as spokesperson, chief of staff and undersecretary, officer in charge of finance, and head of the procuring entity. He testified that he had no personal knowledge of confidential-fund operations and became involved when he received the audit observation memorandum, or A O M."
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "segment_id": "S00404",
          "start_seconds": 4082.31,
          "clock": "01:08:02",
          "speaker_name": "Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr."
        },
        {
          "segment_id": "S00412",
          "start_seconds": 4191.96,
          "clock": "01:09:51",
          "speaker_name": "Atty. Michael Wesley Poa"
        }
      ],
      "heading": "The audit issue",
      "id": "P004",
      "kind": "finding",
      "text": "The A O M identified 15.54 million pesos in informer rewards for the first two quarters as lacking required supporting documents. Referring to the A O M, Poa said the document stated that documentary evidence of success was lacking."
    },
