      "heading": "The court's evidentiary directions",
      "id": "P012",
      "kind": "finding",
      "text": "The chair sustained an objection to a misleading question and limited judicial notice of statements from the House proceedings to the fact that they were made, not their truth. The chair also directed the prosecution to question Poa from the transcript instead of replaying a House member's accusations. Later, the chair sustained an objection to questions about a conversation involving Edward Fajarda, said those questions applied more to Fajarda than to Poa, and told the prosecution to move on."
    },
